Chapter: PondCheck
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Pond
  cites Judge chapter Grade
  cites Gold chapter PondGold

 Grade the Pond port against the gold taken from wasm/pond.zig.

 pond is the FIRST module ported because it holds no arithmetic at all: seven
 outline points, six bank points, six ducks, two colours and a height. Nothing
 here can be wrong for a numerical reason, so a failure means the harness is
 wrong -- which is the whole point of running it first. It tests the loop, not
 the math.

 The tolerance is 0.0, deliberately. Pond's coordinates are integral and its one
 fractional value reaches Codex as the shortest decimal that round-trips the f32,
 re-parsed at f64, so both sides hold the same number exactly. A data seam that
 needs a tolerance is a data seam with a bug in it. The math seams are where a
 tolerance starts earning its keep.

 We say:

Section: Flattening

 Every seam reduces to a flat list so that one grader serves all of them.

  flat-pts : List PondPt, Integer -> List Real
  flat-pts (ps) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ps then []
    else let p = list-at ps i
      in [p.cu, p.cv] & flat-pts ps (i + 1)

  flat-duck-pts : List Duck, Integer -> List Real
  flat-duck-pts (ds) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ds then []
    else let d = list-at ds i
      in [d.p.cu, d.p.cv] & flat-duck-pts ds (i + 1)

  duck-faces : List Duck, Integer -> List Boolean
  duck-faces (ds) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ds then []
    else let d = list-at ds i
      in [d.face-right] & duck-faces ds (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "water-outline " (flat-pts water-outline 0) g-water-outline 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "bank          " (flat-pts bank 0) g-bank 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ducks-p       " (flat-duck-pts ducks 0) g-ducks-p 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "duck-height   " [duck-height] g-duck-height 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "water-color   " [water-color] g-water-color)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "bank-color    " [bank-color] g-bank-color)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "duck-codepoint" [duck-codepoint] g-duck-codepoint)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "ducks-face    " (duck-faces ducks 0) g-ducks-face)
  end
